  "estimatedLength": "35 minutes",
  "objectives": [
    "Identify the four heart chambers, four valves, and major vessels (SVC, IVC, pulmonary arteries/veins, aorta) based on spatial relationships in the heart.",
    "Trace step-by-step the path of blood through the heart and dual-loop circulation, naming chambers, valves, and vessels in order.",
    "Differentiate pulmonary vs systemic circuits and explain how right- vs left-sided heart function supports each loop.",
    "Explain the physiological reason the left ventricle has thicker myocardium than the right ventricle (systemic vs pulmonary pressure demands).",
    "Describe how atrioventricular and semilunar valves prevent backflow during the cardiac cycle."
